sequenceDiagram
    actor U as 👤 Investigador
    participant FE as 🖥️ Frontend
    participant API as 🔌 API
    participant ORC as 🎯 Orchestrator
    participant CEL as 📨 Celery/Redis
    participant NLP as ⚡ NLP Worker
    participant HVY as 🧠 Heavy Worker
    participant FST as ⚡ Fast Worker
    participant LLM as 🤖 LLM (Together.ai)
    participant DB as 🗄️ PostgreSQL

    %% ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
    %% FASE 0: CONFIGURACIÓN DEL PROYECTO
    %% ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

    Note over U,DB: ═══ FASE 0: Configuración del Proyecto ═══

    U->>FE: Crear proyecto
    Note over U,FE: Params:<br/>• nombre (text)<br/>• supuesto_poblacional (text, validated)<br/>• object_of_study (select: concern|emotion|behavior|discourse|identity|custom)<br/>• processing_verb (text, auto-default per type, editable)<br/>• processing_gerund (auto: verb + "ing")<br/>• custom_label (text, solo si object_of_study="custom")<br/>• coding_styles (select, multi: gerundio|in_vivo|nominalizacion|...)

    FE->>API: POST /projects
    Note over API: Validación:<br/>• object_of_study ∈ VALID_OOS<br/>• Si custom → spaCy similarity check<br/>• population → detectar singular (warning)<br/>• processing_verb → conjugar con spaCy<br/>  (plural 3ª persona)

    API->>DB: INSERT proyecto
    DB-->>API: proyecto creado

    API->>FST: f0_population_generalizer (FLASH)
    FST->>LLM: 🟡 FLASH · generalizar población<br/>(pluralizar actores, prohibir unidades)
    LLM-->>FST: {generalized_population, spatial_frame, temporal_frame}
    FST-->>API: OK
    API->>DB: UPDATE population_assumption

    Note over U,FE: 🧬 Population Configuration panel<br/>• Muestra generalized vs original<br/>• Edit inline<br/>• Re-generate button

    U->>FE: Opcional: editar población generalizada
    FE->>API: PUT /projects/{id}/config/population-assumption
    API->>DB: UPDATE population_assumption

    Note over U,FE: 🧪 Nemotrón: generar research question

    U->>FE: Generar research question
    FE->>API: POST /projects/{id}/research-question/generate
    API->>CEL: dispatch research_question_builder → heavy
    CEL->>HVY: fc_research_question_builder (PRO)
    HVY->>DB: SELECT population_assumption, object_of_study
    HVY->>LLM: 🟣 PRO · fc_research_question_builder<br/>Inputs: object_of_study, population_description,<br/>processing_verb, processing_gerund, processing_verb_conjugated
    LLM-->>HVY: {research_question, operational_question,<br/>key_dimensions, rationale}
    Note over LLM: RQ: "What is the CORE [concern] of [population]<br/>      and how do they continuously [resolve] it?"<br/>OQ: "How do [population] [resolve] their CORE [concern]?"
    HVY->>LLM: 🟣 PRO · fc_research_question_critic
    LLM-->>HVY: {verdict: SAT|MOD|FORCED, suggestions}
    HVY->>DB: UPDATE population_assessment.research_question
    HVY-->>CEL: ✅
    API-->>FE: {research_question, operational_question, critic_verdict}

    Note over U,FE: RQ preview editable antes de continuar

    %% ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
    %% FASE A+B: OPEN CODING + CROSS-DOC (lotes de 3 documentos)
    %% ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

    Note over U,DB: ═══ FASE A+B: Open Coding + Cross-Doc (lotes de 3) ═══

    U->>FE: Subir documentos (PDF/TXT/DOCX)
    FE->>API: POST /projects/{id}/documents
    API->>DB: INSERT documentos

    U->>FE: Ejecutar pipeline → open_coding
    FE->>API: POST /projects/{id}/pipeline/run-stage/open_coding
    API->>CEL: dispatch batch_coordinator → heavy

    loop Por lotes de 3 documentos (incluye lote final incompleto)
        Note over HVY: ─── LOTE N: documentos {i} a {i+2} ───

        loop Por cada documento del lote
            CEL->>HVY: process_document_agents_a(doc_id, proyecto_id)

            Note over HVY: Step 0 — Segmentación (spaCy/NLP)
            HVY->>NLP: segmentar_documento
            NLP-->>HVY: segmentos[]

            HVY->>DB: INSERT segmentos

            Note over HVY: Step 0.1 — Glaser Classification (batched PRO)
            HVY->>DB: SELECT segmentos del documento
            HVY->>LLM: 🟣 PRO · fa_glaser_data_classifier<br/>(batch: clasifica baseline|properline|interpreted|vague)
            LLM-->>HVY: {data_type per segmento}
            HVY->>DB: UPDATE segmentos.tipo_dato_glaser

            Note over HVY: Step 0.2 — Pattern & Incident Extraction (unified PRO)
            HVY->>LLM: 🟣 PRO · fa_pattern_incident_extractor<br/>Inputs: {segmentos}, {object_of_study},<br/>{operational_question}, {processing_verb},<br/>{coding_style_instruction}
            Note over LLM: Unified call replacing per-segment extract_incident,<br/>core_pattern_extractor, and prime_mover
            LLM-->>HVY: {incidents[{jot, what_is_this_about, what_category,<br/>what_is_happening, participants_core_concern}],<br/>core_pattern (gerund), pattern_description,<br/>evidence_quotes[2-5], confidence}
            HVY->>DB: INSERT extracted_incidents
            HVY->>DB: UPDATE document_processes.prime_mover

            Note over HVY: A1/A2 — Auxiliary (non-blocking, fire-and-forget)
            HVY->>LLM: 🟣 PRO · fa_population_context (background)
            Note over LLM: Non-blocking auxiliary call
            LLM-->>HVY: {surprising_details, language_patterns}

            HVY->>LLM: 🟣 PRO · fa_process_identifier (background)
            Note over LLM: Non-blocking auxiliary call
            LLM-->>HVY: {process_description}

            HVY-->>CEL: ✅ documento procesado
        end

        Note over HVY: ─── SÍNTESIS CROSS-DOC (lote N) ───

        Note over HVY: B1 — Incident Grouper (AI-only, sin pre-filtro)
        HVY->>DB: SELECT extracted_incidents (lote actual)
        HVY->>LLM: 🟣 PRO · fb_incident_grouper<br/>Inputs: {todos los incidents[]}, {research_question}
        Note over LLM: AI-only grouping:<br/>• NO pairwise comparison<br/>• NO pre-filter por baseline<br/>• El LLM recibe TODOS los incidentes
        LLM-->>HVY: {incident_groups[], ungrouped[]}

        Note over HVY: B2 — Pattern Labeler (per-concept iteration)
        loop Por cada grupo de incidentes
            HVY->>LLM: 🟣 PRO · fb_pattern_labeler<br/>Inputs: {incident_group}, {object_of_study},<br/>{coding_style_instruction}
            Note over LLM: Iteración por concepto, no batch:<br/>• Un grupo → una etiqueta gerundio<br/>• Grounding en incidentes del grupo
            LLM-->>HVY: {proposed_label (gerund), description, anomalies[]}
        end

        Note over HVY: B3 — Label Critic (solo feedback)
        HVY->>LLM: 🟣 PRO · fb_label_critic<br/>(verifica grounding, gerund, scope, overlap)
        Note over LLM: Solo feedback — NO SAT/MOD/FORCED verdicts.<br/>Devuelve observaciones que el investigador revisa.
        LLM-->>HVY: {observations[], coverage_gaps[]}

        Note over HVY: B2.5 — Grounding (incident-based)
        HVY->>DB: SELECT labels con sus incident_groups
        HVY->>LLM: 🟣 PRO · fb_label_grounding<br/>Inputs: {label}, {incident_group[]},<br/>{object_of_study}, {operational_question}
        Note over LLM: Incident-based grounding, no embedding similarity.<br/>Verifica que cada label emerge de los incidentes.
        LLM-->>HVY: {grounding_score, evidence_mapping[], orphan_labels[]}

        HVY->>DB: INSERT categorias (labels aprobadas del lote)

        Note over HVY: ═══ EVERY-3-DOC PAUSE ═══

        Note over HVY: Synthesizer 1 — Category Unification
        HVY->>DB: SELECT all categories (prev + new)
        HVY->>LLM: 🟣 PRO · fd_category_synthesizer
        LLM-->>HVY: {unified_categories[], merges[], renames[]}
        HVY->>DB: UPSERT categories (merge, deduplicate)

        Note over HVY: Synthesizer 2 — Hypothesis Update
        HVY->>DB: SELECT previous hypotheses
        HVY->>LLM: 🟣 PRO · fd_hypothesis_synthesizer
        LLM-->>HVY: {updated_hypotheses[]} (growing note)
        HVY->>DB: UPSERT hypotheses

        Note over HVY: Configuration Critic
        HVY->>LLM: 🟣 PRO · fd_config_critic
        Note over LLM: Reviews: population, concerns, coding style
        LLM-->>HVY: {concerns[], population_variants[], coding_style_rec}

        HVY->>DB: INSERT hitl_decisions (gate: batch_review)
        HVY-->>CEL: 🛑 HITL required
        CEL-->>FE: Redis pub/sub → overlay
        FE-->>U: Modal: review categories, concerns, population, coding style

        U->>FE: Select categories (multi), concerns (multi), population (multi), coding style (single)
        FE->>API: POST /projects/{id}/hitl/batch_review/decide
        API->>DB: Persist decisions (cascada updates)

        HVY-->>CEL: ✅ lote N completo
    end

    %% ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
    %% CORE CATEGORY SELECTION (tras todos los lotes)
    %% ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

    Note over U,DB: ═══ CORE CATEGORY SELECTION ═══

    Note over HVY: 🛡️ Guardrail 1 — Exactly ONE concern confirmed
    HVY->>DB: SELECT concerns confirmados
    Note over HVY: Si ≠ 1 concern → 🛑 HITL: el usuario debe<br/>confirmar exactamente UNA preocupación central

    HVY-->>CEL: 🛑 HITL required (si concerns != 1)
    CEL-->>FE: Redis pub/sub → overlay
    FE-->>U: Modal: confirmar preocupación central<br/>(debe ser exactamente 1)

    U->>FE: Confirm ONE core concern
    FE->>API: POST /projects/{id}/hitl/core_concern/decide
    API->>DB: UPDATE core_concern

    Note over HVY: 🛡️ Guardrail 2 — All categories linked to a concern
    HVY->>DB: SELECT categorias sin link a concern
    Note over HVY: Si hay categorías huérfanas → 🛑 HITL

    HVY-->>CEL: 🛑 HITL required (si categorías huérfanas)
    CEL-->>FE: Redis pub/sub → overlay
    FE-->>U: Modal: vincular categorías huérfanas a concern

    U->>FE: Link orphan categories → concern
    FE->>API: POST /projects/{id}/categories/link-concern
    API->>DB: UPDATE categorias.concern_id

    Note over HVY: Core Category Proposer (hypothesis-inferred)
    HVY->>DB: SELECT categorias, hypotheses, concerns
    HVY->>LLM: 🟣 PRO · fc_core_category_proposer<br/>Inputs: {categorias[]}, {hypotheses[]},<br/>{core_concern}, {object_of_study},<br/>{operational_question}
    Note over LLM: Recomienda core categories basado en<br/>relaciones inferidas desde hipótesis
    LLM-->>HVY: {core_category_candidates[{label, rationale,<br/>hypothesis_links[], confidence}]}

    HVY->>DB: INSERT hitl_decisions (gate: core_category)
    HVY-->>CEL: 🛑 HITL required
    CEL-->>FE: Redis pub/sub → overlay
    FE-->>U: Modal: seleccionar UNA core category

    U->>FE: Select ONE core category
    FE->>API: POST /projects/{id}/hitl/core_category/decide
    API->>DB: UPDATE proyectos.core_category_id

    Note over U,DB: 🔓 Core category seleccionada →<br/>desbloquea selective coding

    %% ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
    %% FASE FC: SELECTIVE CODING
    %% ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

    Note over U,DB: ═══ FASE FC: Selective Coding ═══

    Note over HVY: 🛡️ Guardrail 1: exactly ONE concern confirmed ✓<br/>🛡️ Guardrail 2: all categories linked to concern ✓<br/>🔓 Core category selected → FC unlocked

    U->>FE: Ejecutar pipeline → selective_coding
    FE->>API: POST /projects/{id}/pipeline/run-stage/selective_coding
    API->>CEL: dispatch selective_coding_coordinator → heavy

    CEL->>HVY: selective_coding_coordinator(proyecto_id)

    Note over HVY: FC1 — Main Concern Proposer
    HVY->>DB: SELECT categorias, memos, hypotheses, core_category
    HVY->>LLM: 🟣 PRO · fc_main_concern_proposer<br/>Inputs: {core_category}, {object_of_study},<br/>{research_question}, {operational_question},<br/>{processing_verb}, {coding_style_instruction}
    Note over LLM: Q1: What CORE {object_of_study}s recur?<br/>Q2: How do participants {processing_verb} them?<br/>Q3: Which has most explanatory power?
    LLM-->>HVY: {core_concern (gerund), confidence,<br/>recurring_problems, relevant_population_dimensions}

    Note over HVY: FC2 — Main Concern Critic (feedback only)
    HVY->>LLM: 🟣 PRO · fc_main_concern_critic<br/>(TYPE MATCH + grounding + coverage + abstraction)
    Note over LLM: Feedback only — NO SAT/MOD/FORCED verdicts
    LLM-->>HVY: {observations[], suggestions[]}

    HVY->>DB: INSERT hitl_decisions (gate: selective_coding)
    HVY-->>CEL: 🛑 HITL required
    CEL-->>FE: Redis pub/sub → notificar frontend
    FE-->>U: Modal: revisar selective coding results

    U->>FE: ACCEPT / MODIFY / REJECT
    FE->>API: POST /projects/{id}/hitl/selective_coding/decide

    %% ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
    %% FASE FD: SELECTIVE REDUCTION
    %% ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

    Note over U,DB: ═══ FASE FD: Selective Reduction ═══

    Note over HVY: B1 — Selective Reduction Proposer
    HVY->>LLM: 🟣 PRO · fd_selective_reduction_proposer<br/>Inputs: {core_concern}, {object_of_study},<br/>{core_category}, {all_open_codes}
    Note over LLM: Fase A: filtrar por relevancia al core<br/>"¿Procesa/condiciona/es consecuencia del core?"<br/>Fase B: buscar uniformidades subyacentes<br/>Fase C: reformular conceptos de orden superior
    LLM-->>HVY: {kept[], merged[], discarded[] (con rationale)}

    Note over HVY: B2 — Selective Reduction Critic
    HVY->>LLM: 🟣 PRO · fd_selective_reduction_critic
    LLM-->>HVY: {evaluations[] (false_positives, false_negatives)}

    HVY->>DB: INSERT hitl_decisions (gate: selective_reduction)
    HVY-->>CEL: 🛑 HITL required
    CEL-->>FE: Redis pub/sub → notificar frontend
    FE-->>U: Modal: revisar reducción

    U->>FE: ACCEPT / MODIFY / REJECT
    FE->>API: POST /projects/{id}/hitl/selective_reduction/decide

    %% ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
    %% FASE FE: CORE SATURATION LOOP
    %% ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

    Note over U,DB: ═══ FASE FE: Core Saturation Loop ═══

    loop Por cada categoría × nuevo documento
        HVY->>DB: SELECT paradigm_state, incidentes_nuevos

        Note over HVY: C1 — Core Saturation Proposer
        HVY->>LLM: 🟣 PRO · fe_core_saturation_proposer<br/>Inputs: {category_label}, {category_definition},<br/>{current_paradigm_state}, {new_incidents},<br/>{object_of_study}
        Note over LLM: ¿El incidente revela:<br/>• Nueva propiedad?<br/>• Expansión de gradiente?<br/>• Nueva condición/consecuencia/estrategia?
        LLM-->>HVY: {proposed_expansions[], did_state_expand}

        Note over HVY: C2 — Core Saturation Critic
        HVY->>LLM: 🟡 FLASH · fe_core_saturation_critic<br/>(verifica que la expansión sea genuina, no ruido)
        LLM-->>HVY: {verdict: SAT|MOD|FORCED}

        HVY->>DB: UPDATE paradigm_states

        Note over HVY: Paradigm Integrator
        HVY->>LLM: 🟣 PRO · fe_paradigm_integrator<br/>Inputs: {current_paradigm}, {new_incidents},<br/>{object_of_study}
        LLM-->>HVY: {did_state_expand, expansion_type}
        HVY->>DB: INSERT paradigm_states (versioned)
    end

    Note over HVY: Panel de 4 señales (sin LLM)
    HVY->>DB: SELECT saturation_metrics<br/>(rolling_std, consecutive_no_expand,<br/>property_coverage, incident_density)
    HVY-->>CEL: ✅ saturation loop complete

    %% ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
    %% FASE FF: DATABASE A/B
    %% ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

    Note over U,DB: ═══ FASE FF: Database A/B ═══

    Note over HVY: D1 — Database A Proposer (NODES)
    HVY->>DB: SELECT categorias saturadas, core_category
    HVY->>LLM: 🟣 PRO · ff_database_a_proposer<br/>Inputs: {saturated_categories}, {core_category},<br/>{object_of_study}, {research_question}
    Note over LLM: Fase A: identificar core node<br/>Fase B: clasificar (condition|consequence|strategy|dimension)<br/>Fase C: compilar definiciones desde propiedades
    LLM-->>HVY: {nodes[{label, entity_type, definition,<br/>is_core, grounding_incidents}]}

    Note over HVY: D2 — Database A Critic
    HVY->>LLM: 🟣 PRO · ff_database_a_critic<br/>(5 criterios: entity_type, grounding, abstraction,<br/>incidents, core identification)
    LLM-->>HVY: {node_evaluations[], system_issues}

    HVY->>DB: INSERT hitl_decisions (gate: database_a)
    HVY-->>CEL: 🛑 HITL required

    U->>FE: ACCEPT database_a
    FE->>API: POST /projects/{id}/hitl/database_a/decide

    HVY->>DB: INSERT database_nodes

    Note over HVY: D3 — Database B Proposer (EDGES)
    HVY->>LLM: 🟣 PRO · ff_database_b_proposer<br/>Inputs: {nodes}, {conceptual_relationships},<br/>{hypotheses}, {object_of_study}, {core_concern}
    Note over LLM: 7 tipos canónicos:<br/>PROCESSES (obligatorio), LEADS_TO,<br/>IS_A_STRATEGY_FOR, IS_A_CONSEQUENCE_OF,<br/>IS_A_CONDITION_FOR, VARIES_WITH, CO_OCCURS_WITH
    LLM-->>HVY: {edges[{source, target, relationship_type,<br/>evidence, direction, strength}]}

    Note over HVY: D4 — Database B Critic
    HVY->>LLM: 🟣 PRO · ff_database_b_critic<br/>(contradictions, missing edges, orphan nodes)
    LLM-->>HVY: {edge_evaluations[], system_issues}

    HVY->>DB: INSERT hitl_decisions (gate: database_b)
    HVY-->>CEL: 🛑 HITL required

    U->>FE: ACCEPT database_b
    FE->>API: POST /projects/{id}/hitl/database_b/decide

    HVY->>DB: INSERT database_edges

    %% ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
    %% FASE 6b: THEORETICAL PLAYGROUND
    %% ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

    Note over U,DB: ═══ FASE 6b: Theoretical Playground ═══

    HVY->>DB: UPDATE proyectos.estado = 'playground_ready'
    HVY->>CEL: dispatch prepare_playground → heavy

    Note over HVY: Seed: 12 theoretical coding families
    HVY->>DB: INSERT theoretical_codes (si no existen)

    Note over HVY: Ghost Blob Mapper
    HVY->>LLM: 🟣 PRO · f6b_ghost_blob_mapper<br/>(memas huérfanos → sugerir categoría)
    LLM-->>HVY: {suggested_category, confidence}
    HVY->>DB: INSERT ghost_blobs

    Note over HVY: Memo Theoretical Tagger
    loop Por cada memo del proyecto
        HVY->>LLM: 🟡 FLASH · f6b_memo_theoretical_tagger<br/>Inputs: {memo_content}, {object_of_study}
        Note over LLM: 12 familias canónicas:<br/>Causes, Consequences, Conditions, Process,<br/>Degree, Dimension, Type, Strategy,<br/>Structural, Functional, Interaction, Identity
        LLM-->>HVY: {family_affinities[{family, score}],<br/>primary_family, secondary_family}
        HVY->>DB: UPDATE memos.metadata
    end

    Note over HVY: Ecosystem Gap Detection
    HVY->>DB: SELECT COUNT ghost_blobs sin link
    opt >= 3 unlinked ghosts
        HVY->>LLM: 🟣 PRO · f6b_gap_alerter<br/>Inputs: {core_concern}, {object_of_study},<br/>{gaps_summary}
        LLM-->>HVY: {gaps[], alerts[]}
    end

    HVY-->>CEL: ✅ playground ready

    %% ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
    %% FASE 6a: REDACCIÓN NATURAL
    %% ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

    Note over U,DB: ═══ FASE 6a: Redacción Natural ═══

    U->>FE: Iniciar redacción (sorting group)
    FE->>API: POST /writing/write-section
    API->>CEL: dispatch write_section → heavy

    HVY->>DB: SELECT memos ordenados (sorting group)
    HVY->>DB: SELECT object_of_study, research_question, core_concern

    Note over HVY: Writer
    HVY->>LLM: 🟣 PRO · f6a_natural_writer<br/>Inputs: {memos_ordered}, {object_of_study},<br/>{research_question}, {core_concern}
    Note over LLM: Reglas:<br/>• Presente conceptual<br/>• Conceptos como sujetos<br/>• Gerundios para procesos<br/>• Abstracción progresiva
    LLM-->>HVY: {draft, citations[], concepts[], orphan_memos[]}

    Note over HVY: Writing Critic
    HVY->>LLM: 🟣 PRO · f6a_writing_critic
    LLM-->>HVY: {verdict: SAT|MOD|FORCED, issues[]}

    Note over HVY: Gap Feeler (background, non-blocking)
    HVY->>LLM: 🟡 FLASH · f6a_gap_feeler<br/>Inputs: {draft}, {object_of_study}, {core_concern}
    Note over LLM: Detecta:<br/>• MISSING_EVIDENCE<br/>• UNDERDEVELOPED_PROPERTY<br/>• DISCONNECTED_CATEGORY<br/>• CONCEPTUAL_LEAP<br/>• ORPHAN_CLAIM
    LLM-->>HVY: {gaps[{type, description, severity}]}

    HVY-->>FE: {draft, critique, gaps}

    %% ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
    %% FASE 6c: DIÁLOGO CON LITERATURA
    %% ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

    Note over U,DB: ═══ FASE 6c: Diálogo con Literatura ═══

    U->>FE: Comparar con literatura
    FE->>API: POST /literature/compare
    API->>CEL: dispatch compare_literature → heavy

    HVY->>DB: SELECT teoría completa (cats + hyps + props)
    HVY->>LLM: 🟣 PRO · f6c_literature_comparer<br/>Inputs: {theory}, {literature_fragments},<br/>{object_of_study}, {research_question}
    Note over LLM: Literatura como datos, no autoridad.<br/>EXTENDS | MODIFIES | INTEGRATES | TRANSCENDS
    LLM-->>HVY: {comparison_table[]}

    HVY->>LLM: 🟣 PRO · f6c_literature_critic<br/>(detecta forcing, authority bias, name-dropping)
    LLM-->>HVY: {verdict, issues[]}

    HVY-->>FE: {comparison_table, critique}

    %% ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
    %% FASE 6d: APLICABILIDAD
    %% ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

    Note over U,DB: ═══ FASE 6d: Aplicabilidad ═══

    U->>FE: Generar guías de aplicabilidad
    FE->>API: POST /applicability/generate
    API->>CEL: dispatch generate_applicability → heavy

    HVY->>DB: SELECT teoría completa
    HVY->>LLM: 🟣 PRO · f6d_applicability_engine<br/>Inputs: {theory}, {application_context},<br/>{object_of_study}
    Note over LLM: Identifica:<br/>• Variables de control (modificables)<br/>• Variables de acceso (condicionantes)<br/>• Guías de intervención<br/>• Implicaciones
    LLM-->>HVY: {control_variables[], access_variables[],<br/>guidelines[], implications[], future_agenda[]}

    HVY->>LLM: 🟣 PRO · f6d_applicability_critic<br/>(genuineness, limits, accessibility, modifiability)
    LLM-->>HVY: {verdict, issues[]}

    HVY-->>FE: {guidelines, critique}

    %% ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
    %% FASE 6e: FINAL REPORT
    %% ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

    Note over U,DB: ═══ FASE 6e: Final Report ═══

    U->>FE: Generar reporte final
    FE->>API: POST /projects/{id}/pipeline/run-stage/final_report
    API->>CEL: dispatch final_report → heavy

    HVY->>DB: SELECT todos los datos acumulados:<br/>object_of_study, research_question, core_concern,<br/>core_category, database_nodes, database_edges,<br/>hypotheses, population_description,<br/>literature_dialogue, applicability_guidelines

    HVY->>LLM: 🟣 PRO · f6a_final_report<br/>Inputs: {object_of_study}, {research_question},<br/>{core_concern}, {core_category}, {nodes}, {edges},<br/>{hypotheses}, {population_description},<br/>{literature_dialogue}, {applicability_guidelines},<br/>{processing_verb}, {processing_gerund},<br/>{Pattern} (→ {object_of_study})
    Note over LLM: 8 secciones:<br/>1. Abstract (200w)<br/>2. Core {object_of_study}<br/>3. Core Category<br/>4. Theoretical Model<br/>5. Population Dimensions<br/>6. Literature Dialogue<br/>7. Applicability<br/>8. Research Trajectory
    LLM-->>HVY: {report: {title, abstract, core_pattern,<br/>core_category, theoretical_model,<br/>population_dimensions, literature_dialogue,<br/>applicability, research_trajectory}}

    HVY->>DB: INSERT final_reports (graceful if table missing)

    HVY-->>CEL: ✅ terminal node
    CEL-->>FE: report complete
    FE-->>U: 📄 Reporte final generado

    Note over U,DB: ═══ FIN DEL PIPELINE ═══

    %% ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
    %% FLUJOS TRANSVERSALES
    %% ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

    Note over U,DB: ═══ Transversal: HITL Gates ═══
    Note over U,FE: Gates en orden:<br/>1. batch_review 🔄 (cada 3 docs)<br/>2. core_concern 🎯<br/>3. core_category ⭐<br/>4. selective_coding 🔍<br/>5. selective_reduction ✂️<br/>6. database_a 🗄️<br/>7. database_b 🔗
    Note over U,FE: Cada gate: Accept → avanza / Modify → re-ejecuta / Reject → pausa

    Note over U,DB: ═══ Transversal: Experimental Mode ═══
    Note over U,FE: 🧪 Cambiar object_of_study mid-project<br/>→ estado vuelve a "coding"<br/>→ pipeline se reinicia desde open coding

    Note over U,DB: ═══ Transversal: AbortableTask ═══
    Note over CEL,HVY: Todas las tareas Celery usan AbortableTask<br/>→ tracking en pipeline_tasks<br/>→ cancelación segura
